 the logic in a beginner-readable order: guard the start tile, remove the last tile, set the new current tile, clear completion, render, then update the debug text.","type":"text"}]}],"mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia"}],"anchor":"Undo-the-last-tile"},{"stepsSection":[{"type":"step","code":"06-StageCatalog.swift","runtimePreview":null,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StageCatalog"},{"type":"text","text":" that returns a small list of boards."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"caption":[],"media":"preview-placeholder.svg"},{"type":"step","code":null,"runtimePreview":null,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each stage readable: title, boardSize, start tile, goal tile, and blocked tiles."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"caption":[],"media":null}],"title":"Use 3x3 cube stages","contentSection":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The earlier 2x2 board is a learning step. It keeps the relationship between ","type":"text"},{"code":"SKTileMapNode","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"SKTileSet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"SKTileGroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" easy to see.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the cube version, make every playable stage 3x3. The same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BoardPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" structure expands the SpriteKit tile map and SceneKit touch conversion when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"boardSize"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"3"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add two or three 3x3 stages now. Do not build every possible cube-face relationship yet. The goal is to switch between a few playable puzzles on neighboring faces."}]}],"mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia"}],"anchor":"Use-3x3-cube-stages"},{"stepsSection":[{"type":"step","code":null,"runtimePreview":null,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the undo code feels long, keep it long for now. This tutorial favors clarity before compression."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"caption":[],"media":null}],"title":"Check the result","contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You should be able to undo a move, finish a 3x3 stage, then continue into another 3x3 stage on a neighboring cube face."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"anchor":"Check-the-result"}],"kind":"tasks"},{"featuredEyebrow":"Tutorial","title":"07. Put SpriteKit on a SceneKit Cube","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Put SpriteKit puzzle scenes on multiple faces of an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SCNBox"},{"type":"text","text":", then convert a 3D surface tap into the current stage’s 2D tile coordinate."}],"action":{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","overridingTitle":"Get started","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"Get started","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.example.CubeOneStrokePuzzle\/tutorials\/Cube-One-Stroke-Puzzle\/07-SceneKit-Cube-Material-And-Texture-Touch"},"kind":"callToAction"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.example.CubeOneStrokePuzzle\/tutorials\/Cube-One-Stroke-Puzzle\/06-SwiftUI-Undo-And-Three-By-Three","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"category":"Cube One-Stroke Puzzle","title":"06. Add Undo and Expand Stages","categoryPathComponent":"CubeOneStrokePuzzle","role":"project"},"kind":"project","variants":[{"paths":["\/tutorials\/cube-one-stroke-puzzle\/06-swiftui-undo-and-three-by-three"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://com.example.CubeOneStrokePuzzle/tutorials/Cube-One-Stroke-Puzzle/01-SpriteKit-Scene-And-Container-Layers#Create-the-scene-file":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.example.CubeOneStrokePuzzle\/tutorials\/Cube-One-Stroke-Puzzle\/01-SpriteKit-Scene-And-Container-Layers